+// nekocore: installed by the nekocore module (src/EraHitCrit.cpp). Given the
+// source of a combat-rating bonus -- exactly one of `spell` (a SPELL_AURA_MOD_RATING
+// aura), `item` (a generic hit/crit stat in item_template) or `enchant` (one in
+// SpellItemEnchantment) -- and the ratings it adds to (1 << CombatRating), returns
+// the subset that source's 1.12 form did not affect: 3.0 merged 1.12's separate
+// melee/ranged and spell hit/crit bonuses into one rating. The answer depends
+// only on the source, never on the player, so applying and removing a bonus
+// always agree. Null when the module is not loaded, which leaves stock behaviour.
+extern uint32 (*g_nekoVanillaExcludedRatings)(SpellInfo const* spell, ItemTemplate const* item, SpellItemEnchantmentEntry const* enchant, uint32 ratingMask);
